Z||000006||northstar87||03-10-2001||08:36 AM||||Hello Archie,<BR>   I guess I failed to mention that I would have never done any other installation because the Northstar install was the best thing that I ever did.  It is fast,(I know that yours are faster) I still have all of my trunk, only gained 200 lbs total in the install, air conditioning, cruise control, NEVER overheats, I can keep axles in my cars, and NEVER have to worry about blowing up transmissions.  I also get 24 miles per gallon on the highway.  You should know the guy I am working with.  John Lingenfelter.  If he can't do it nobody can.  Thanks for reading and I hope I see you in Florida.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Archie||03-10-2001||09:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by northstar87:<BR><B>Hello Archie,<BR>    John Lingenfelter.  If he can't do it nobody can.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, I totally agree with your whole statement. I too can say "I still have all of my trunk, only gained (less than) 200 lbs total in the install, air conditioning, cruise control, NEVER overheats, I can keep axles in my cars, and NEVER have to worry about blowing up transmissions.  I also get 24 miles per gallon on the highway." You stated all of the above items as if they were deviations from the SBC swap car. And you know that none of those items are issues with a properly done SBC swap.<P>My question didn't have anything to do with the items you list.<P>My questions remain.... WHAT is the "it" that John is trying to fix? , Why has it been 4 years looking for an answer? <P>Simple questions.<P>Thanks<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jay||03-10-2001||09:11 AM||||Thanks Northstar87, I've had help from John Norman and the guys at Howell.  I love my Northstar engine and to be honest it was almost easy to do.  Like you said I know it's got more potential. For a bone stock engine I guess 13's is okay but I was expecting times in the 12's.  When I go over the line I'm doing about 100mph.  It feels like I have no top end, off the line I can smoke anyone. check me out at <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jay||03-10-2001||09:52 AM||||Hi Archie,<BR>"It" is a feeling while driving the car that there is a whole lot more in that engine.  I believe that the Traction Control in the Caddy ECM is looking for a reading from the sensors.  They aren't there so the computer goes into a saftey mode cutting power.  That's what I believe is happening, but I really don't know much about reprogramming computers.  Does that sound right Northstar87?  I've tried adding the TCM to the harness with limited success, it's better but not like what it's full potential should be.  I went with the Northstar because it is still relatively rare to find one in a Fiero.  In fact I'm the first in Canada to have one up and running.  No regrets here.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||03-10-2001||10:21 AM||||I think it's the hi tech aspect of it all. I mean the N* is as close as you will get to a Zr1 fiero. 4 cam 32 valve. Most of these guys are running 13's with only 70% of their total HP output. The N* is made to run hotter than a small block , remember the old ad campaigns with the N* running 50 miles with no engine coolant?? The N* has a progressive power band as well , doesn't drop off at 5000 rpm like most small blocks.  You don't have to worry about the tranny snaping in half, engine and tranny are made for each other.<P>But too each his own , for some pople the small block floats their Boat ,for some it's the N*.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000011||terryk||03-10-2001||10:45 AM||||What year is this Northstar and what ECM is being used?<P>I'd be surprise if lack of ABS pulses for the traction control really limits the power. ABS and TC are usually benign. There are errors for the loss of the serial data but someone is saying the power is limited?<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 03-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Jay||03-10-2001||12:12 PM||||The engine is a 97 STS.  I've converted the engine to a 95 (Throttle body, o2 sensors and TPS)  The computer is a 95 with a 94 Prom (This is the best set up according to John Norman).  It has a true dual exhaust.  It retains the power steering pump and A/C compressor.  These two items will be removed this month and a shorter belt installed.  I just didn't have time to remove them last year, I wanted to get the car up and running first.  Now I can tinker with tuning.||||reg||1
