Z||000016||Will||03-10-2001||10:29 PM||||I'm in the process on doing a Getrag Northstar conversion. I've discovered a few things (bear in mind that I haven't <I>tested</I> these ideas yet, but see no reason that they shouldn't work):<P>1) Oldsmobile Aurora V8 ECM has SAME part number as Cadillac ECM. The only difference between these two systems is the chip. A $34 Aurora chip should run the Northstar if the fuel pressure is turned up to ~57 psi. Since you guys are using the pig (4T80E) it won't even throw transmission codes.<P>2) The Olds/Caddy ECM sends a duty cycle modulated square wave representing delivered torque to the TC computer, and the TC computer sends one back representing desired torque. Both signals use 90% duty cycle for 100% torque. Route the delivered torque output from the ECM into the desired torque input on the ECM. That should solve any difficulties traction control may present.<P>3) Both ECM's have routines to reduce engine torque if certain "abusive manuevers" are detected. The shop manuals don't say what these maneuvers are, but this might be hindering your launches.<P>4) The Caddy ignition control module looks at CKS an CMS outputs and sends the ECM three signals: a 24x pulse train, a 4x pulse train, and a 1/2x pulse train (once per cam revolution) which the ECM uses to determine crankshaft position.<BR>The LS1 crank position sensor module sends its ECM a 24x signal and a 4x signal. The LS1 cam position sensor module sends the ECM a 1x per cam revolution signal.<BR>WILD SPECULATION: if the two 24x singals look sufficiently similar, the two 4x signals are the same, and the 1/2x signals are the same, then a remapped LS1 ECM might be able to control a Northstar through use of the Caddy ignition control module and LS1 coil-near-plug setup.<P>Any thoughts terryk?||||reg||1
Z||000017||Will||03-10-2001||10:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by northstar87:<BR><B><BR>It is a 13 second car all day long right as it sits.  There is more in there.  Trust me.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hehehehehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Get the wild heads and cams package from <A HREF="http://www.chrfab.com" TARGET=_blank>www.chrfab.com</A>  <BR>Wind the engine out to 8500 on a stock-as-the-day-it-rolled-off-the-line shortblock without any fear that it will fly apart.<BR>If you don't break into the 12's then... your car must be a dud. I'd be willing to take it off your hands with no hassle  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
