Z||000028||Will||03-12-2001||11:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>Will, do you work for GM?  I've looked for wiring diagrams in all of the books (Hayes, Chilton) with no success in finding anything on Traction Control or specifically the TCM itself.  I've tried going to a Cadillac dealer but they are not interested in letting me photocopy pages from their shop manuals.  Do you have access to such info?  Has anyone else tried the Aurora chip out there?  Has anyone tried the LS1 chip as stated earlier?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I don't work for GM, but I am friendly with the local Olds dealer. That's how I was able to look at the Aurora shop manual. I bought the '95 Cadillac manual. It's pretty steep at 130 USD, but the insight it can give into the operation of the systems is worth it. Haynes and Chilton's are OK for mechanical stuff, but have no insight into the electonic systems. Helm is the only way to go for this information.<BR>The OBDI ('95) Aurora chip is the one I was suggesting.<BR>I think it's a safe bet no one outside GM has tried the LS1 controller.||||reg||1
